A||||8||GT Bastard||Diff between 4 &5 speed Isuzu tranny??||||1||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||03-16-2000||07:36 PM||||I've found a very experienced Fiero nut/mechanic that has done several auto to manual swaps and I'm thinking of having him do one for me.  The only manual tranny he has right now is a 4sp Isuzu from a 4cyl... I've already seen the durability debate, but I'm just curious if the durability is the same between 4 and 5 sp. Isuzu trannies.  The gear ratio in the one he has is 4.10, which would kick some major ass.  Do you think it's worth it to try and find a Getrag?<BR>thanks all..||||reg||1
Z||000001||DRH||03-16-2000||07:46 PM||||The 4 speed from the 84 4 cyl is actually a Muncie. The 85 and some 86 V6s had a 4 speed Muncie also (a different one though). Late 86-88 V6s had the Getrag (also made by Muncie). The only Isuzu is the 5 speed in 85-88 4cyl.<P>I have heard of people using the 84 tranny because of the 4.10 gearing. I think general consensus (if there is such a thing) is that the 84 4spd is stronger than the Isuzu 5spd but not quite as strong as the V6 4spd or Getrag 5spd.<P>At any rate the 4.10 with a V6 should give you a he!! of a shot off the line. <p>[This message has been edited by DRH (edited 03-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||03-16-2000||07:51 PM||||Thanks for the info... That's basically what he told me, but I didn't really want to take his word for it. 4.10 gears, here I come!!!  Forget highway driving, but around town is going to rock.||||reg||1
Z||000003||pherder||03-16-2000||08:57 PM||||GT Bastard,<P>Ed Parks (The Fiero Factory) is running around in a 85 Fiero with a 3.4 and that 4.10 4 speed!<P>He has posted on the lists that he is VERY happy with the combo!  <P>If you want out of the hole acceleration, the 4.10 FDR transaxle is what you want.  If you want gas mileage, get the Isuzu 5 speed with the 3.34 FDR.  Of course you could always spend the $$$ and get a 3.83 or 4.11 FDR for the Isuzu later (at $300+ AND install fees!!)<P>Paul<p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 03-16-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000004||WKDFIRO||03-16-2000||11:10 PM||||From what we have seen the 84 4 cyl case is the weak point. The gears are fine. Its just the case that can crack. The final gear with the 4.10 is happily sitting in the 4 spd 86 SE of Keith Huff (Fiero Motorsports). Up until recently we would have said the Isuzu 5 speed was not strong enough for a V6 but one customer had to have one and seems to be holding up just fine.<BR>I have an 85 GT now but before I had the 5 spd Isuzu. I would go for the 5 speed for the mileage myself. Here in LA its all freeways.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 03-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||DRH||03-17-2000||03:36 PM||||GT Bastard,<P>Check out this link for info on all the trannys complete with all gear ratios. Highway probably won't be much worse than a V6 4 speed. It will actually be better than some of the automatics (multiply high gear times final drive... the lower the better for highway).<P>To get off the line ratio multiply 1st times final drive. 14.5 for the 4.10, 12.5 for the Getrag, 12.1 for the V6 4 speed, 13.6 for the V6 4 speed tranny w/4.10 final drive transplant (wkdfiero).<P>With a little more math you can even figure your shift points.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Oh... Make sure the tranny in question <B>is</B> a 4.10. Not all 84s were. If you have it out you can put it in 1st gear... input shaft should turn (about) 14.5 times for the axle to turn once.<P> <A HREF="http://www.mindspring.com/~fierosketch/osg/tranny.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mindspring.com/~fierosketch/osg/tranny.html</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by DRH (edited 03-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Spyder||03-17-2000||04:24 PM||||On my 84, I took out the 4 speed, even though quicker 0-60 times and opted for the Isuzu 5 speed.  With the 4 speed it always seemed like it needed to shift out. Since I installed the V8 I need a little better gas mileage. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||88 Fiero||03-17-2000||05:11 PM||||For anyone who is interested in going to a 5-Speed Izusu tranny or the 5-Speed Getrag tranny... I ran a website that modify this tranny for performance...and they have that available to our cars for both 4 cylinder and 6 cylinder. interested let me know and I will give you their website... Really interesting tho...||||reg||1
Z||000008||GT Bastard||03-17-2000||08:15 PM||||Does anybody know what the max. torque rating for a muncie 4-sp????||||reg||1
